# draft with backslash  [technical-reviewer]  want: allow
  $ echo x > .eccode\drafts\a.json
  old        : deny: technical-reviewer reviews/designs but does not edit project files; write drafts under .ec
  new        : deny: technical-reviewer reviews/designs but does not edit project files; write drafts under .ec
  new/win32  : deny: technical-reviewer reviews/designs but does not edit project files; write drafts under .ec

# platform override without ECCODE_TEST=1 must be ignored (target would read as relative + cd => deny if win32 were honoured... no: on linux a bare C:\ path tokenizes to C:Users..., which path.posix treats as relative; with a cd that is a deny)
  $ cd /tmp && echo x > C:\Users\me\notes.txt  [technical-reviewer]
  new, ECCODE_GUARD_PLATFORM=win32, ECCODE_TEST unset : deny: This command changes directory (cd/pushd/popd) and then writes the relative path "C:Usersm   (expected: deny = linux reading, override ignored)
  new, ECCODE_GUARD_PLATFORM=win32, ECCODE_TEST=1     : deny: This command changes directory (cd/pushd/popd) and then writes the relative path "C:Usersm   (expected: allow = win32 reading)
  new, ECCODE_GUARD_PLATFORM=linux, ECCODE_TEST=1     : deny: This command changes directory (cd/pushd/popd) and then writes the relative path "C:Usersm   (expected: deny)
